module
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Noetherian.Defs
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Quotient.Operations
public import Sheaf.RingTheory.SingularIdeal
import Sheaf.RingTheory.PopescuLifting

@[expose] public section
universe u v w z
namespace Algebra

/-- The lifting part of Stacks 07F0, before desingularization. It provides the
compatible fourth-power quotient map, the singular-ideal element, and the comparison
of singular ideals needed by the final application of 07CT. No strictly standard
hypothesis or factorization through a desingularized algebra is asserted here.

Source: Stacks Project, Smoothing Ring Maps, Lemma 07CP applied with `π ^ 4`, and the
prime-ideal verification in Lemma 07F0 (blueprint: new-popescu-lifting-witness).

Proof: The annihilator hypotheses imply Ann(π^n) = Ann(π) for all positive n:
if xπ^(n+1) = 0, apply Ann(π²) = Ann(π) to xπ^(n-1), then induct.
Thus 07CP applies with π⁴ and π⁸. It gives a finitely presented D, δ : D → Λ,
and ρ : C → D/π⁴D commuting with reduction to Λ/π⁴Λ. Compose ρ with σ and the
projection from A. This composite kills π⁴ and therefore induces the asserted φ;
the commuting diagram and hfactor give its compatibility on representatives.
By 07CP(b), every nonsmooth prime of D contains π. Since H_{D/R} is radical
with precisely the nonsmooth zero locus, π belongs to H_{D/R}.
Put J = H_{D/R}Λ. Its radical contains π, so any prime p containing J contains
π and gives primes modulo π⁴ and π⁸. The inverse image of p/π⁴Λ under ρ is
also the inverse image of p/π⁸Λ under τ, by the commuting diagram. If this
prime of C were smooth over R/π⁸R, 07CP(c) would make δ⁻¹(p) smooth over R,
contrary to H_{D/R} ⊆ δ⁻¹(p). Hence H_C maps into p/π⁸Λ. Every lift of an
element of τ(H_C) is consequently in every prime containing J, hence in √J.
Mapping √J to Λ/π⁸Λ gives an ideal (the quotient map is surjective), so it
contains the ideal generated by τ(H_C). This proves the last inclusion.
The argument uses no nontriviality assumption; if π is a unit the relevant
quotients are zero, and if π is nilpotent the off-π smooth locus is empty. -/
theorem popescu_lifting_witness
    (R : Type u) (A : Type v) (Λ : Type w)
    [CommRing R] [CommRing A] [CommRing Λ]
    [Algebra R A] [Algebra R Λ] [IsNoetherianRing R]
    (π : R)
    (hAnnR : Module.annihilator R (Ideal.span ({π} : Set R)) =
      Module.annihilator R (Ideal.span ({π ^ 2} : Set R)))
    (hAnnΛ : Module.annihilator Λ (Ideal.span ({algebraMap R Λ π} : Set Λ)) =
      Module.annihilator Λ (Ideal.span ({(algebraMap R Λ π) ^ 2} : Set Λ)))
    (α : A →ₐ[R] Λ) [FinitePresentation R A]
    (C : Type z) [CommRing C]
    [Algebra (R ⧸ Ideal.span ({π ^ 8} : Set R)) C]
    [FinitePresentation (R ⧸ Ideal.span ({π ^ 8} : Set R)) C]
    (σ : (A ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R A) (Ideal.span ({π ^ 8} : Set R)))
      →ₐ[R ⧸ Ideal.span ({π ^ 8} : Set R)] C)
    (τ : C →ₐ[R ⧸ Ideal.span ({π ^ 8} : Set R)]
      (Λ ⧸ Ideal.map (algebraMap R Λ) (Ideal.span ({π ^ 8} : Set R))))
    (hfactor : ∀ a : A,
      τ (σ (Ideal.Quotient.mk
        (Ideal.map (algebraMap R A) (Ideal.span ({π ^ 8} : Set R))) a)) =
        Ideal.Quotient.mk
          (Ideal.map (algebraMap R Λ) (Ideal.span ({π ^ 8} : Set R))) (α a)) :
    ∃ (D : Type (max u z)) (_ : CommRing D) (_ : Algebra R D),
      FinitePresentation R D ∧ ∃ (δ : D →ₐ[R] Λ),
        (∃ φ : (A ⧸ Ideal.span {(algebraMap R A π) ^ 4}) →ₐ[R]
            (D ⧸ Ideal.span {(algebraMap R D π) ^ 4}),
          ∀ (a : A) (d : D),
            φ (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ a) = Ideal.Quotient.mk _ d →
            Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {(algebraMap R Λ π) ^ 4}) (α a) =
              Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {(algebraMap R Λ π) ^ 4}) (δ d)) ∧
        algebraMap R D π ∈ singularIdeal R D ∧
        Ideal.map τ.toRingHom (singularIdeal (R ⧸ Ideal.span ({π ^ 8} : Set R)) C) ≤
          Ideal.map
            (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.map (algebraMap R Λ) (Ideal.span ({π ^ 8} : Set R))))
            (Ideal.map δ.toRingHom (singularIdeal R D)).radical := by
  sorry

end Algebra
